            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-WTvOdgvkTo9timxYvu8l12uGgwf\">Regarding Egypt and Saudi Arabia, these two countries allocate the majority of their water to agriculture, at 82% and 64% respectively. Their industrial water usage shows a notable difference, with Saudi Arabia's figure of 30% being three times higher than Egypt's 10%. As for domestic consumption, both countries record single-digit percentages, with Egypt at 8% and Saudi Arabia slightly lower at 6%.</div>\n</div>",
