            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-SE1Bd7MWGobHFlxG4jwlz8QVgDg\">In terms of the remaining countries, Canada and New Zealand demonstrate contrasting patterns, with industry being their primary water consumer. Canada's industrial usage is significantly higher at 70%, compared to New Zealand's 46%. Agricultural water consumption in New Zealand stands at 44%, which is more than four times higher than Canada's mere 10%. Domestic use in these two countries is relatively higher than in the Middle Eastern nations, with Canada recording 20% and New Zealand 10%.</div>\n</div>",
